fixed a.azl:22:29 E0120 `;` does not end a statement in azoL; the end of the line does
fixed a.azl:1:1 E0126 azoL has no `use`; a program is the files named to `azol build`, and what is built in needs no import
fixed a.azl:2:1 E0126 azoL has no `pub`; every declaration is seen by the whole program
fixed a.azl:2:14 E0123 azoL has no references; a value is passed and named as itself, and a parameter is read-only unless it says `mut`
fixed a.azl:2:17 E0122 type parameters and type arguments are written between `[ ]` in azoL, not `< >`
fixed a.azl:3:5 E0121 `let mut` is Rust; in azoL a variable that changes is declared with `var`
fixed a.azl:11:16 E0122 type parameters and type arguments are written between `[ ]` in azoL, not `< >`
fixed a.azl:11:24 E0124 azoL has no macros; a list is written `[1, 2, 3]`, without `vec!`
fixed a.azl:12:19 E0123 azoL has no references; a value is passed and named as itself, and a parameter is read-only unless it says `mut`
fixed a.azl:13:5 E0124 azoL has no macros; `print` takes one value, and values go into a text as `"total: {sum}"`
fixed a.azl:14:14 E0128 `and` is written `&&` in azoL
fixed a.azl:16:7 E0127 `elif` is written `else if` in azoL
fixed a.azl:16:19 E0128 azoL has no `===` and no `!==`; values are compared with `==` and `!=`
fixed a.azl:19:21 E0125 `String::from(...)` is Rust; a text between quotes is already a `str` of its own
fixed a.azl:2:14 E0220 `Vec` is not an azoL type; the list that grows is `List[T]`
fixed a.azl:2:28 E0220 `i32` is not an azoL type; the integer type is `i64`
fixed a.azl:11:13 E0220 `Vec` is not an azoL type; the list that grows is `List[T]`
fixed a.azl:4:16 E0223 `.iter()` is not azoL: there are no iterators; a list is looped over as it is and has its methods directly, such as `xs.sum()`
fixed a.azl:14:17 E0128 `not` is written `!` in azoL
fixed a.azl:15:9 E0221 `console.log` is not azoL; `print` writes a value and ends the line
fixed a.azl:15:24 E0224 `+` joins two texts and does not turn a number into one; write `str(n)`, or put the value in the text: `"n = {n}"`
fixed a.azl:17:15 E0221 `len(x)` is not azoL; the length of a list, a text or a map is the method `x.len()`
fixed a.azl:19:12 E0220 `String` is not an azoL type; text is `str`
fixed a.azl:20:13 E0223 `.length` is called `.len` in azoL
fixed a.azl:21:13 E0223 `.clone()` is not needed: in azoL a value is copied when it is given a second name, and moved when the first is not used again
fixed a.azl:21:14 E0223 `.size` is called `.len` in azoL
