==== `fix --check` writes nothing and ends with 1 when there is work
---- file a.azl
fn main() {
    let mut n = 1;
    n += 1
    print(n)
}
---- run fix --check a.azl
---- exit 1
---- stdout
would fix a.azl:2:18 E0120 `;` does not end a statement in azoL; the end of the line does
would fix a.azl:2:5 E0121 `let mut` is Rust; in azoL a variable that changes is declared with `var`
---- stderr
2 to fix, 0 left
---- after a.azl
fn main() {
    let mut n = 1;
    n += 1
    print(n)
}
==== a file with a mistake that has no edit is not written
---- file a.azl
fn main() {
    let mut n = 1;
    let m = null
    print(n)
}
---- run fix a.azl
---- exit 1
---- stdout
not written: a.azl:2:18 E0120 `;` does not end a statement in azoL; the end of the line does
not written: a.azl:2:5 E0121 `let mut` is Rust; in azoL a variable that changes is declared with `var`
---- stderr
error[E0222]: azoL has no `null`; a value that may be absent is an `Option[T]`, and absent is `None`
 --> a.azl:3:13
  |
3 |     let m = null
  |             ^
0 fixed, 2 not written, 1 left; 1 file not written because a mistake in it has no edit (`--partial` writes what could be done)
